---
description: Nopnapat's defaults for every project
alwaysApply: true
---

## Answers
- Keep answers short and lead with the code. No restating the question.
- End with one line on what you did not check or run, if anything.

## Tooling
- Use pnpm by default. If the repo has another lockfile, use that tool and never mix.
- Use the Node version from `.nvmrc` when there is one.
- Prefer what the project already has (installed deps, existing utils, components) over adding something new. Say why before adding a dependency.
- Follow the repo's ESLint and Prettier config. Don't reformat code you didn't change.
- Before calling a change done, run the project's existing typecheck, lint and test scripts for what you touched.

## Git
- Commit messages: `type(*): message`, lowercase, imperative. Types: feat, fix, refactor, docs, test, chore, ci.
- Only commit when asked. Never push, force-push or switch branches unless asked.

## Secrets
- Never read, print or edit `.env` files, keys or tokens. Edit `.env.example` instead and leave values for me.
